  "composition_summary": "Preserved the volatile tail unchanged (single user request, no justified repair). Drafted one class-22 pure-logic component pc-contrast-07: it reads raw records via inputs.get('records') (never direct access), validates that records is a nonempty list of 1..3 objects each with exactly code (string length 2..5) and enabled (exact bool), and returns {ok, records} with records echoed only when valid else []. No imports/host/IO, no upstream validation assumption, no exceptions or coercion, no Markdown in content. The body assigns result on every branch (invalid -> {'ok': False, 'records': []}, valid -> {'ok': True, 'records': records}). This is an unapproved target-interface draft; activation requires Q1, human Q2 and runtime typed-runner support, which are not claimed.",
  "adjusted_volatile_messages": [["user", "Prepare the requested reusable draft without executing any operation."]],
  "settings_adjustments": [],
  "proposed_components": [
    {
      "class_code": 22,
      "payload": {
        "name": "pc-contrast-07",
        "description": "Pure-logic guard: validate a raw list of 1..3 records, each with exactly code (string length 2..5) and enabled (exact bool), and return {ok, records} echoing the original list only when valid. No I/O, imports, host calls or upstream validation assumption. Empty, missing, null, wrong-type, extra-field or out-of-range inputs yield {ok: false, records: []} without exceptions or coercion.",
        "content": "def classify_records(records):\n    if not (type(records) is list and 1 <= len(records) <= 3):\n        result = {'ok': False, 'records': []}\n    else:\n        valid = True\n        for rec in records:\n            if not (type(rec) is dict and set(rec.keys()) == {'code', 'enabled'}\n                    and type(rec['code']) is str and 2 <= len(rec['code']) <= 5\n                    and type(rec['enabled']) is bool):\n                valid = False\n                break\n        if not valid:\n            result = {'ok': False, 'records': []}\n        else:\n            result = {'ok': True, 'records': records}\n    return result\nresult = classify_records(inputs.get('records'))"
      }
    }
  ]
